# west has only a double tap. Tapped once, the window of the double tap runs
# out (multiTapMs, 220 ms) and the tap has no action: a decision, no output.
+west@0 -west@30
# Tapped twice, it is the double tap.
+west@500 -west@530 +west@600 -west@630
# north has a tap and a triple tap. Tapped twice, the window runs out at a
# count of two, which has no action. Tapped once, it is the tap.
+north@1000 -north@1030 +north@1100 -north@1130
+north@1600 -north@1630
# west is tapped once and south pressed inside the window: the press ends the
# window.
+west@2000 -west@2030 +south@2100 -south@2130
# east (timeOnly, hold at 400 ms) is pending when west is tapped once: west's
# edges wait in the buffer and replay when east is released as a tap, at 3300,
# after the window west's release opened at 3030 is over (3250). The window
# is decided at the replay.
+east@3000 +west@3010 -west@3030 -east@3300
# leftshoulder has a press action next to its double tap. Tapped once, the
# press ran its action and answered the cycle: the end of the window has nothing
# more to decide.
+leftshoulder@4000 -leftshoulder@4030
